organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"4776067582b399a74bc434030f60589af4d4b11d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/the-omega-institute/trureturing/commits/4776067582b399a74bc434030f60589af4d4b11d","html_url":"https://github.com/the-omega-institute/trureturing/commit/4776067582b399a74bc434030f60589af4d4b11d"},{"sha":"922925339b182b503358b24524cdea131065f53b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/the-omega-institute/trureturing/commits/922925339b182b503358b24524cdea131065f53b","html_url":"https://github.com/the-omega-institute/trureturing/commit/922925339b182b503358b24524cdea131065f53b"}],"stats":{"total":1158,"additions":1145,"deletions":13},"files":[{"sha":"cb4f394c74ba24c4284f13b1051820c719e226e9","filename":"Blueprint/D5/S1/Recurrence/OEISA400644.md","status":"modified","additions":24,"deletions":11,"changes":35,"blob_url":"https://github.com/the-omega-institute/trureturing/blob/3a382196d3b69fec4a2ba29a7468eca5e9844034/Blueprint%2FD5%2FS1%2FRecurrence%2FOEISA400644.md","raw_url":"https://github.com/the-omega-institute/trureturing/raw/3a382196d3b69fec4a2ba29a7468eca5e9844034/Blueprint%2FD5%2FS1%2FRecurrence%2FOEISA400644.md","contents_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/the-omega-institute/trureturing/contents/Blueprint%2FD5%2FS1%2FRecurrence%2FOEISA400644.md?ref=3a382196d3b69fec4a2ba29a7468eca5e9844034","patch":"@@ -4,7 +4,19 @@\n \n The exact rounded three-term norm sequence has the Tribonacci square-root ratio limit.\n \n-**Definition 1.1 (Source integer rounding operation).**\n+**Theorem 1.1 (Integer threshold and nearest real rounding agree).**\n+\n+$$\\forall s: \\mathbb{N}, \\operatorname{round}\\left(\\operatorname{Real}.\\operatorname{sqrt}\\left((s: \\mathbb{R})\\right)\\right) = (\\operatorname{sourceRound}\\left(s\\right): \\mathbb{Z})$$\n+\n+*Proof.* Machine-checked in Lean as `D5/S1/Recurrence/OEISA400644.sourceRound_round` (`✓ std3`). ∎\n+\n+*Source.* Repository-derived.\n+\n+*Commentary.*\n+\n+For every natural radicand s, rounding its real square root gives the integer cast of sourceRound s. The strict half-unit error excludes ties.\n+\n+**Definition 1.2 (Source integer rounding operation).**\n \n Lean statement: `D5/S1/Recurrence/OEISA400644.sourceRound`\n \n@@ -16,7 +28,7 @@ Lean statement: `D5/S1/Recurrence/OEISA400644.sourceRound`\n \n For every nonnegative integer radicand s, Nat.sqrt s is the lower integer candidate and the threshold s > r²+r selects r+1. This is the exact integer operation in the published Python source.\n \n-**Theorem 1.2 (Two integer candidates bracket every source radicand).**\n+**Theorem 1.3 (Two integer candidates bracket every source radicand).**\n \n Lean statement: `D5/S1/Recurrence/OEISA400644.sourceRound_spec`\n \n@@ -28,7 +40,7 @@ Lean statement: `D5/S1/Recurrence/OEISA400644.sourceRound_spec`\n \n The integer square root brackets s between r² and (r+1)², and sourceRound s is exactly r or r+1.\n \n-**Theorem 1.3 (Strict half-unit source rounding error).**\n+**Theorem 1.4 (Strict half-unit source rounding error).**\n \n Lean statement: `D5/S1/Recurrence/OEISA400644.sourceRound_real_error`\n \n@@ -40,7 +52,7 @@ Lean statement: `D5/S1/Recurrence/OEISA400644.sourceRound_real_error`\n \n Integer radicands cannot have a half-integer square root. Consequently the source operation differs from the real square root by strictly less than one half for every nonnegative integer radicand.\n \n-**Definition 1.4 (The zero-based source sequence).**\n+**Definition 1.5 (The zero-based source sequence).**\n \n Lean statement: `D5/S1/Recurrence/OEISA400644.a`\n \n@@ -52,7 +64,7 @@ Lean statement: `D5/S1/Recurrence/OEISA400644.a`\n \n The sequence starts 0, 0, 1 and applies the published rounded square-root recurrence at every later index. Source index n≥1 is represented by a(n−1).\n \n-**Theorem 1.5 (Exact recurrence at every index).**\n+**Theorem 1.6 (Exact recurrence at every index).**\n \n Lean statement: `D5/S1/Recurrence/OEISA400644.a_recurrence`\n \n@@ -64,7 +76,7 @@ Lean statement: `D5/S1/Recurrence/OEISA400644.a_recurrence`\n \n For every natural n, a(n+3) is exactly sourceRound of the sum of the three preceding squares.\n \n-**Theorem 1.6 (The source sequence is monotone).**\n+**Theorem 1.7 (The source sequence is monotone).**\n \n Lean statement: `D5/S1/Recurrence/OEISA400644.a_mono`\n \n@@ -76,7 +88,7 @@ Lean statement: `D5/S1/Recurrence/OEISA400644.a_mono`\n \n Each term is at least the preceding term. This follows from the lower square-root candidate in the exact source rounding operation.\n \n-**Theorem 1.7 (Eventual denominator positivity).**\n+**Theorem 1.8 (Eventual denominator positivity).**\n \n Lean statement: `D5/S1/Recurrence/OEISA400644.a_pos`\n \n@@ -88,7 +100,7 @@ Lean statement: `D5/S1/Recurrence/OEISA400644.a_pos`\n \n Every term from the third zero-based term onward is at least one, so the eventual consecutive ratios have positive denominators.\n \n-**Theorem 1.8 (Uniqueness of the recursively constructed sequence).**\n+**Theorem 1.9 (Uniqueness of the recursively constructed sequence).**\n \n Lean statement: `D5/S1/Recurrence/OEISA400644.a_unique`\n \n@@ -100,7 +112,7 @@ Lean statement: `D5/S1/Recurrence/OEISA400644.a_unique`\n \n Any natural-valued sequence with the same three initial values and the same exact recurrence agrees pointwise with a.\n \n-**Theorem 1.9 (The Tribonacci square-root is the largest positive sextic root).**\n+**Theorem 1.10 (The Tribonacci square-root is the largest positive sextic root).**\n \n Lean statement: `D5/S1/Recurrence/OEISA400644.rho_is_largest_positive_root`\n \n@@ -112,7 +124,7 @@ Lean statement: `D5/S1/Recurrence/OEISA400644.rho_is_largest_positive_root`\n \n rho is the positive square root of the Tribonacci constant. It satisfies rho⁶−rho⁴−rho²−1=0, and every positive real root of this polynomial is at most rho.\n \n-**Definition 1.10 (Full infinite ratio limit target).**\n+**Definition 1.11 (Full infinite ratio limit target).**\n \n Lean statement: `D5/S1/Recurrence/OEISA400644.targetClaim`\n \n@@ -124,7 +136,7 @@ Lean statement: `D5/S1/Recurrence/OEISA400644.targetClaim`\n \n The claim includes the infinite limit of a(n+3)/a(n+2), root identification, the exact positive-index recurrence, uniqueness on positive indices, positive denominators, and the same ratio limit for every sequence satisfying the published initial data and recurrence.\n \n-**Theorem 1.11 (The exact infinite consecutive-ratio limit).**\n+**Theorem 1.12 (The exact infinite consecutive-ratio limit).**\n \n Lean statement: `D5/S1/Recurrence/OEISA400644.result`\n \n@@ -163,6 +175,7 @@ The theorem-specific typed registrations retain their compiled evidence. Source\n - Truth anchor: `D5/S1/Recurrence/OEISA400644.rho_is_largest_positive_root`\n - Truth anchor: `D5/S1/Recurrence/OEISA400644.sourceRound`\n - Truth anchor: `D5/S1/Recurrence/OEISA400644.sourceRound_real_error`\n+- Truth anchor: `D5/S1/Recurrence/OEISA400644.sourceRound_round`\n - Truth anchor: `D5/S1/Recurrence/OEISA400644.sourceRound_spec`\n - Truth anchor: `D5/S1/Recurrence/OEISA400644.targetClaim`\n - Dependency: [D5/S0/Tower/Tribonacci/PerronRoot](../../S0/Tower/Tribonacci/PerronRoot.md)"},{"sha":"27115f1f125b125163bf8544d394d7c835a48749","filename":"Blueprint/D5/S1/Recurrence/OEISA400644.scribe.cs","status":"modified","additions":22,"deletions":0,"changes":22,"blob_url":"https://github.com/the-omega-institute/trureturing/blob/3a382196d3b69fec4a2ba29a7468eca5e9844034/Blueprint%2FD5%2FS1%2FRecurrence%2FOEISA400644.scribe.cs","raw_url":"https://github.com/the-omega-institute/trureturing/raw/3a382196d3b69fec4a2ba29a7468eca5e9844034/Blueprint%2FD5%2FS1%2FRecurrence%2FOEISA400644.scribe.cs","contents_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/the-omega-institute/trureturing/contents/Blueprint%2FD5%2FS1%2FRecurrence%2FOEISA400644.scribe.cs?ref=3a382196d3b69fec4a2ba29a7468eca5e9844034","patch":"@@ -6,11 +6,33 @@ namespace StrataLint.Scribe.Blueprint.D5.S1.Recurrence;\n internal sealed class OEISA400644Document : IScribeDocumentDefinition\n {\n     private const string Prefix = \"D5/S1/Recurrence/OEISA400644.\";\n+    private static Formula Parenthesized(Formula value) => Seq(Open, value, Close);\n \n     public DocumentDefinition Create() => DocumentDefinition.Create(ScribeNode.Create(\n         \"The exact rounded three-term norm sequence has the Tribonacci square-root ratio limit.\",\n         H(\"OEIS A400644: exact rounded recurrence\"),\n         Blocks(\n+            Describe.Lean(\n+                DescribeId.Create(\"oeis-a400644-round-agreement\"),\n+                DeclarationHandle.Create(Prefix + \"sourceRound_round\"),\n+                H(\"Integer threshold and nearest real rounding agree\"),\n+                StatementSource.FromAuthor(Disp(Seq(\n+                    Forall, Sp, FormulaDsl.Id(\"s\"), Colon, Sp,\n+                    Seq(Mathbb, Grp(FormulaDsl.Id(\"N\"))), Comma, Sp,\n+                    new Formula.Relation(\n+                        new Formula.Apply(Seq(Operatorname, Grp(FormulaDsl.Id(\"round\"))), [\n+                            new Formula.Apply(Seq(Operatorname, Grp(FormulaDsl.Id(\"Real\")), Dot,\n+                                Operatorname, Grp(FormulaDsl.Id(\"sqrt\"))), [\n+                                Parenthesized(Seq(FormulaDsl.Id(\"s\"), Colon, Sp,\n+                                    Mathbb, Grp(FormulaDsl.Id(\"R\"))))])]),\n+                        FormulaRelationOperator.Equal,\n+                        Parenthesized(Seq(new Formula.Apply(Seq(Operatorname,\n+                            Grp(FormulaDsl.Id(\"sourceRound\"))), [FormulaDsl.Id(\"s\")]),\n+                            Colon, Sp, Mathbb, Grp(FormulaDsl.Id(\"Z\")))))))),\n+                AssessedProvenance.FromRepo(),\n+                Blocks(Paragraph(Text(\n+                    \"For every natural radicand s, rounding its real square root gives the integer cast of sourceRound s. The strict half-unit error excludes ties.\"))),\n+                DescribeRole.Theorem),\n             Describe.Lean(\n                 DescribeId.Create(\"oeis-a400644-source-round\"),\n                 DeclarationHandle.Create(Prefix + \"sourceRound\"),"},{"sha":"e48394d7193bc258f79e5951962d78a4754450cd","filename":"Blueprint/D5/S1/Recurrence/OEISA400645.md","status":"added","additions":95,"deletions":0,"changes":95,"blob_url":"https://github.com/the-omega-institute/trureturing/blob/3a382196d3b69fec4a2ba29a7468eca5e9844034/Blueprint%2FD5%2FS1%2FRecurrence%2FOEISA400645.md","raw_url":"https://github.com/the-omega-institute/trureturing/raw/3a382196d3b69fec4a2ba29a7468eca5e9844034/Blueprint%2FD5%2FS1%2FRecurrence%2FOEISA400645.md","contents_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/the-omega-institute/trureturing/contents/Blueprint%2FD5%2FS1%2FRecurrence%2FOEISA400645.md?ref=3a382196d3b69fec4a2ba29a7468eca5e9844034","patch":"@@ -0,0 +1,95 @@\n+# Bernáth's OEIS A400645 consecutive-ratio limit\n+\n+## Abstract\n+\n+The signed four-lag rounded norm sequence has Bernáth's exact ratio limit.\n+\n+**Definition 1.1 (The signed four-square radicand).**\n+\n+$$\\forall a: (\\mathbb{N} \\to \\mathbb{N}), \\forall n: (\\mathbb{N}), \\operatorname{radicand}\\left(a, n\\right) = ((\\operatorname{a}\\left(n\\right): \\mathbb{Z}))^{2} + ((\\operatorname{a}\\left(n - 1\\right): \\mathbb{Z}))^{2} + ((\\operatorname{a}\\left(n - 2\\right): \\mathbb{Z}))^{2} - ((\\operatorname{a}\\left(n - 3\\right): \\mathbb{Z}))^{2}$$\n+\n+*Formalization.* `D5/S1/Recurrence/OEISA400645.radicand` (`✓ std3`).\n+\n+*Citation.* Bence Bernáth (2026). *OEIS A400645, signed four-lag rounded norm ratio*. URL: <https://oeis.org/A400645>.\n+\n+*Commentary.*\n+\n+a(n+1) = round(sqrt(a(n)^2 + a(n-1)^2 + a(n-2)^2 - a(n-3)^2)). Source: OEIS A400645, revision 21, NAME field (unpaginated). The four squares are integers; the predecessor indices use natural subtraction.\n+\n+**Definition 1.2 (The positive-index recurrence and initial values).**\n+\n+$$\\forall a: (\\mathbb{N} \\to \\mathbb{N}), \\operatorname{IsSourceSequence}\\left(a\\right) = ((\\operatorname{a}\\left(1\\right) = 0) \\land ((\\operatorname{a}\\left(2\\right) = 0) \\land ((\\operatorname{a}\\left(3\\right) = 0) \\land ((\\operatorname{a}\\left(4\\right) = 1) \\land (\\forall n: (\\mathbb{N}), (4 \\le n) \\Rightarrow ((0 \\le \\operatorname{radicand}\\left(a, n\\right)) \\land ((\\operatorname{a}\\left(n + 1\\right): \\mathbb{Z}) = \\operatorname{round}\\left(\\operatorname{Real}.\\operatorname{sqrt}\\left((\\operatorname{radicand}\\left(a, n\\right): \\mathbb{R})\\right)\\right))))))))$$\n+\n+*Formalization.* `D5/S1/Recurrence/OEISA400645.IsSourceSequence` (`✓ std3`).\n+\n+*Citation.* Bence Bernáth (2026). *OEIS A400645, signed four-lag rounded norm ratio*. URL: <https://oeis.org/A400645>.\n+\n+*Commentary.*\n+\n+a(n+1) = round(sqrt(a(n)^2 + a(n-1)^2 + a(n-2)^2 - a(n-3)^2)). The Mathematica field states a[1] == a[2] == a[3] == 0, a[4] == 1. Source: OEIS A400645, revision 21, NAME and Mathematica fields (unpaginated). The recurrence applies for n ≥ 4; index zero is unused. Nonnegativity of the signed radicand is explicit.\n+\n+**Definition 1.3 (The cross-referenced quartic constant).**\n+\n+$$(squaredLimit: \\mathbb{R}) = \\frac{1 + \\operatorname{Real}.\\operatorname{sqrt}\\left(13\\right) + \\operatorname{Real}.\\operatorname{sqrt}\\left(2 \\cdot \\operatorname{Real}.\\operatorname{sqrt}\\left(13\\right) - 2\\right)}{4}$$\n+\n+*Formalization.* `D5/S1/Recurrence/OEISA400645.squaredLimit` (`✓ std3`).\n+\n+*Citation.* Bence Bernáth (2026). *OEIS A400645, signed four-lag rounded norm ratio*. URL: <https://oeis.org/A400645>.\n+\n+*Commentary.*\n+\n+Equals (1 + sqrt(13) + sqrt(2*sqrt(13) - 2))/4. - _Vaclav Kotesovec_, Aug 27 2021. Source: OEIS A289917, revision 48, FORMULA field (unpaginated), cross-referenced by A400645.\n+\n+**Definition 1.4 (The conjectured consecutive-ratio limit).**\n+\n+$$(limitingRatio: \\mathbb{R}) = \\operatorname{Real}.\\operatorname{sqrt}\\left(squaredLimit\\right)$$\n+\n+*Formalization.* `D5/S1/Recurrence/OEISA400645.limitingRatio` (`✓ std3`).\n+\n+*Citation.* Bence Bernáth (2026). *OEIS A400645, signed four-lag rounded norm ratio*. URL: <https://oeis.org/A400645>.\n+\n+*Commentary.*\n+\n+Numerical evidence suggests that the ratio of consecutive terms (a(n+1)/a(n)) tends to 1.3122819079... (sqrt(A289917)) which is the largest real root of the asymptotic equation of this sequence: x^8-x^6-x^4-x^2+1. Source: OEIS A400645, revision 21, COMMENTS field (unpaginated). The value sqrt(A289917) is Real.sqrt squaredLimit.\n+\n+**Definition 1.5 (The full infinite limit and largest-root assertion).**\n+\n+$$claim = ((\\exists a: (\\mathbb{N} \\to \\mathbb{N}), \\operatorname{IsSourceSequence}\\left(a\\right)) \\land ((\\forall a: (\\mathbb{N} \\to \\mathbb{N}), (\\operatorname{IsSourceSequence}\\left(a\\right)) \\Rightarrow (\\forall e: (\\mathbb{R}), (0 < e) \\Rightarrow (\\exists N: (\\mathbb{N}), (4 \\le N) \\land (\\forall n: (\\mathbb{N}), (N \\le n) \\Rightarrow ((0 < \\operatorname{a}\\left(n\\right)) \\land (\\lvert \\frac{(\\operatorname{a}\\left(n + 1\\right): \\mathbb{R})}{(\\operatorname{a}\\left(n\\right): \\mathbb{R})} - limitingRatio \\rvert < e)))))) \\land (((limitingRatio)^{8} - (limitingRatio)^{6} - (limitingRatio)^{4} - (limitingRatio)^{2} + 1 = 0) \\land (\\forall x: (\\mathbb{R}), ((x)^{8} - (x)^{6} - (x)^{4} - (x)^{2} + 1 = 0) \\Rightarrow (x \\le limitingRatio)))))$$\n+\n+*Formalization.* `D5/S1/Recurrence/OEISA400645.claim` (`✓ std3`).\n+\n+*Citation.* Bence Bernáth (2026). *OEIS A400645, signed four-lag rounded norm ratio*. URL: <https://oeis.org/A400645>.\n+\n+*Commentary.*\n+\n+Numerical evidence suggests that the ratio of consecutive terms (a(n+1)/a(n)) tends to 1.3122819079... (sqrt(A289917)) which is the largest real root of the asymptotic equation of this sequence: x^8-x^6-x^4-x^2+1. This is related to A116732 where the asymptotic equation is y^4-y^3-y^2-y+1 via y=x^2. Source: OEIS A400645, revision 21, COMMENTS field (unpaginated). Natural indices start at 1. Subtraction in the radicand is in ℤ, and nearest rounding produces an integer. Existence, eventual positive denominators and the largest real root are included.\n+\n+**Theorem 1.6 (The signed rounded recurrence has the stated infinite limit).**\n+\n+$$(\\exists a: (\\mathbb{N} \\to \\mathbb{N}), \\operatorname{IsSourceSequence}\\left(a\\right)) \\land ((\\forall a: (\\mathbb{N} \\to \\mathbb{N}), (\\operatorname{IsSourceSequence}\\left(a\\right)) \\Rightarrow (\\forall e: (\\mathbb{R}), (0 < e) \\Rightarrow (\\exists N: (\\mathbb{N}), (4 \\le N) \\land (\\forall n: (\\mathbb{N}), (N \\le n) \\Rightarrow ((0 < \\operatorname{a}\\left(n\\right)) \\land (\\lvert \\frac{(\\operatorname{a}\\left(n + 1\\right): \\mathbb{R})}{(\\operatorname{a}\\left(n\\right): \\mathbb{R})} - limitingRatio \\rvert < e)))))) \\land (((limitingRatio)^{8} - (limitingRatio)^{6} - (limitingRatio)^{4} - (limitingRatio)^{2} + 1 = 0) \\land (\\forall x: (\\mathbb{R}), ((x)^{8} - (x)^{6} - (x)^{4} - (x)^{2} + 1 = 0) \\Rightarrow (x \\le limitingRatio))))$$\n+\n+*Proof.* Machine-checked in Lean as `D5/S1/Recurrence/OEISA400645.result` (`✓ std3`). ∎\n+\n+*Resolves.* `Problems/bernath-a400645` (proved) by `D5/S1/Recurrence/OEISA400645.result`.\n+\n+<!-- scribe-open-problem-resolution-v1 {\"problem_slug\":\"bernath-a400645\",\"declaration_gid\":\"D5/S1/Recurrence/OEISA400645.result\",\"resolution_kind\":\"proved\"} -->\n+\n+*Source.* Repository-derived.\n+\n+*Acknowledgement.* Bence Bernáth (2026). *OEIS A400645, signed four-lag rounded norm ratio*. URL: <https://oeis.org/A400645>.\n+\n+*Commentary.*\n+\n+The integer rounding bound and monotonicity give a Fibonacci upper estimate. With squaredLimit greater than 17/10, the rounding errors grow more slowly than the dominant mode. The exact value a(26)=324 controls the entire infinite error tail and gives a positive normalized projection limit above 73872/17. A weighted three-coordinate contraction gives a positive limit for normalized squares. Division and continuity of Real.sqrt give the consecutive-ratio limit. The quartic factorization identifies the largest octic root.\n+\n+## References\n+\n+- Truth anchor: `D5/S1/Recurrence/OEISA400645.IsSourceSequence`\n+- Truth anchor: `D5/S1/Recurrence/OEISA400645.claim`\n+- Truth anchor: `D5/S1/Recurrence/OEISA400645.limitingRatio`\n+- Truth anchor: `D5/S1/Recurrence/OEISA400645.radicand`\n+- Truth anchor: `D5/S1/Recurrence/OEISA400645.result`\n+- Truth anchor: `D5/S1/Recurrence/OEISA400645.squaredLimit`\n+- Dependency: [D5/S0/Tower/NonPisotFrontier/BetaThirteen](../../S0/Tower/NonPisotFrontier/BetaThirteen.md)\n+- Dependency: [D5/S1/Recurrence/ComplementaryGoldenRatioLimit](ComplementaryGoldenRatioLimit.md)\n+- Dependency: [D5/S1/Recurrence/OEISA400644](OEISA400644.md)"},{"sha":"ef44ef3fca239d44dadcd49cb8bb6d62b7e8d11a","filename":"Blueprint/D5/S1/Recurrence/OEISA400645.scribe.cs","status":"added","additions":110,"deletions":0,"changes":110,"blob_url":"https://github.com/the-omega-institute/trureturing/blob/3a382196d3b69fec4a2ba29a7468eca5e9844034/Blueprint%2FD5%2FS1%2FRecurrence%2FOEISA400645.scribe.cs","raw_url":"https://github.com/the-omega-institute/trureturing/raw/3a382196d3b69fec4a2ba29a7468eca5e9844034/Blueprint%2FD5%2FS1%2FRecurrence%2FOEISA400645.scribe.cs","contents_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/the-omega-institute/trureturing/contents/Blueprint%2FD5%2FS1%2FRecurrence%2FOEISA400645.scribe.cs?ref=3a382196d3b69fec4a2ba29a7468eca5e9844034","patch":"@@ -0,0 +1,110 @@\n+using static StrataLint.Scribe.DefinitionDsl;\n+using static StrataLint.Scribe.FormulaDsl;\n+using F = StrataLint.Scribe.FormulaDsl;\n+\n+namespace StrataLint.Scribe.Blueprint.D5.S1.Recurrence;\n+\n+internal sealed class OEISA400645Document : IScribeDocumentDefinition\n+{\n+    private const string Prefix = \"D5/S1/Recurrence/OEISA400645.\";\n+    private static readonly LibraryNoteRef Source = LibraryNoteRef.Create(\"D5/L/Eigenstructure/oeis2026a400645\");\n+\n+    public DocumentDefinition Create() => DocumentDefinition.Create(ScribeNode.Create(\n+        \"The signed four-lag rounded norm sequence has Bernáth's exact ratio limit.\",\n+        H(\"Bernáth's OEIS A400645 consecutive-ratio limit\"),\n+        Blocks(\n+            Node(\"radicand\", \"The signed four-square radicand\",\n+                All(\"a\", SequenceType(), All(\"n\", Nat(), Equal(Call(\"radicand\", V(\"a\"), V(\"n\")), RadicandBody()))),\n+                \"a(n+1) = round(sqrt(a(n)^2 + a(n-1)^2 + a(n-2)^2 - a(n-3)^2)). Source: OEIS A400645, revision 21, NAME field (unpaginated). The four squares are integers; the predecessor indices use natural subtraction.\",\n+                DescribeRole.Definition, AssessedProvenance.FromLiterature(Source)),\n+            Node(\"IsSourceSequence\", \"The positive-index recurrence and initial values\",\n+                All(\"a\", SequenceType(), Equal(Call(\"IsSourceSequence\", V(\"a\")), Parenthesized(SourceBody()))),\n+                \"a(n+1) = round(sqrt(a(n)^2 + a(n-1)^2 + a(n-2)^2 - a(n-3)^2)). The Mathematica field states a[1] == a[2] == a[3] == 0, a[4] == 1. Source: OEIS A400645, revision 21, NAME and Mathematica fields (unpaginated). The recurrence applies for n ≥ 4; index zero is unused. Nonnegativity of the signed radicand is explicit.\",\n+                DescribeRole.Definition, AssessedProvenance.FromLiterature(Source)),\n+            Node(\"squaredLimit\", \"The cross-referenced quartic constant\",\n+                Equal(Cast(V(\"squaredLimit\"), Real()),\n+                    Divide(Add(Add(D(1), SqrtOf(D(1,3))), SqrtOf(Sub(Mul(D(2), SqrtOf(D(1,3))), D(2)))), D(4))),\n+                \"Equals (1 + sqrt(13) + sqrt(2*sqrt(13) - 2))/4. - _Vaclav Kotesovec_, Aug 27 2021. Source: OEIS A289917, revision 48, FORMULA field (unpaginated), cross-referenced by A400645.\",\n+                DescribeRole.Definition, AssessedProvenance.FromLiterature(Source)),\n+            Node(\"limitingRatio\", \"The conjectured consecutive-ratio limit\",\n+                Equal(Cast(V(\"limitingRatio\"), Real()), SqrtOf(V(\"squaredLimit\"))),\n+                \"Numerical evidence suggests that the ratio of consecutive terms (a(n+1)/a(n)) tends to 1.3122819079... (sqrt(A289917)) which is the largest real root of the asymptotic equation of this sequence: x^8-x^6-x^4-x^2+1. Source: OEIS A400645, revision 21, COMMENTS field (unpaginated). The value sqrt(A289917) is Real.sqrt squaredLimit.\",\n+                DescribeRole.Definition, AssessedProvenance.FromLiterature(Source)),\n+            Node(\"claim\", \"The full infinite limit and largest-root assertion\",\n+                Equal(V(\"claim\"), Parenthesized(ClaimBody())),\n+                \"Numerical evidence suggests that the ratio of consecutive terms (a(n+1)/a(n)) tends to 1.3122819079... (sqrt(A289917)) which is the largest real root of the asymptotic equation of this sequence: x^8-x^6-x^4-x^2+1. This is related to A116732 where the asymptotic equation is y^4-y^3-y^2-y+1 via y=x^2. Source: OEIS A400645, revision 21, COMMENTS field (unpaginated). Natural indices start at 1. Subtraction in the radicand is in ℤ, and nearest rounding produces an integer. Existence, eventual positive denominators and the largest real root are included.\",\n+                DescribeRole.Definition, AssessedProvenance.FromLiterature(Source)),\n+            Node(\"result\", \"The signed rounded recurrence has the stated infinite limit\",\n+                ClaimBody(),\n+                \"The integer rounding bound and monotonicity give a Fibonacci upper estimate. With squaredLimit greater than 17/10, the rounding errors grow more slowly than the dominant mode. The exact value a(26)=324 controls the entire infinite error tail and gives a positive normalized projection limit above 73872/17. A weighted three-coordinate contraction gives a positive limit for normalized squares. Division and continuity of Real.sqrt give the consecutive-ratio limit. The quartic factorization identifies the largest octic root.\",\n+                DescribeRole.Theorem, AssessedProvenance.FromRepo(Source),\n+                new OpenProblemResolutionClaim(ProblemSlugRef.Create(\"bernath-a400645\"), ResolutionKind.Proved)))));\n+\n+    private static Formula RadicandBody() => Sub(\n+        Add(Add(Pow(Cast(Call(\"a\", V(\"n\")), Int()), D(2)),\n+            Pow(Cast(Call(\"a\", Sub(V(\"n\"), D(1))), Int()), D(2))),\n+            Pow(Cast(Call(\"a\", Sub(V(\"n\"), D(2))), Int()), D(2))),\n+        Pow(Cast(Call(\"a\", Sub(V(\"n\"), D(3))), Int()), D(2)));\n+\n+    private static Formula SourceBody()\n+    {\n+        var a = V(\"a\");\n+        var n = V(\"n\");\n+        var rounded = Call(\"round\", SqrtOf(Cast(Call(\"radicand\", a, n), Real())));\n+        var step = And(Le(D(0), Call(\"radicand\", a, n)),\n+            Equal(Cast(Call(\"a\", Add(n, D(1))), Int()), rounded));\n+        var recurrence = All(\"n\", Nat(), Imp(Le(D(4), n), step));\n+        return And(Equal(Call(\"a\", D(1)), D(0)),\n+            And(Equal(Call(\"a\", D(2)), D(0)),\n+                And(Equal(Call(\"a\", D(3)), D(0)),\n+                    And(Equal(Call(\"a\", D(4)), D(1)), recurrence))));\n+    }\n+\n+    private static Formula ClaimBody()\n+    {\n+        var a = V(\"a\");\n+        var n = V(\"n\");\n+        var ratio = Divide(Cast(Call(\"a\", Add(n, D(1))), Real()),\n+            Cast(Call(\"a\", n), Real()));\n+        var error = Lt(Abs(Sub(ratio, V(\"limitingRatio\"))), V(\"e\"));\n+        var tail = All(\"n\", Nat(), Imp(Le(V(\"N\"), n),\n+            And(Lt(D(0), Call(\"a\", n)), error)));\n+        var threshold = ExistsOf(\"N\", Nat(), And(Le(D(4), V(\"N\")), tail));\n+        var convergence = All(\"a\", SequenceType(), Imp(Call(\"IsSourceSequence\", a),\n+            All(\"e\", Real(), Imp(Lt(D(0), V(\"e\")), threshold))));\n+        var algebraic = And(Equal(Octic(V(\"limitingRatio\")), D(0)),\n+            All(\"x\", Real(), Imp(Equal(Octic(V(\"x\")), D(0)), Le(V(\"x\"), V(\"limitingRatio\")))));\n+        return And(ExistsOf(\"a\", SequenceType(), Call(\"IsSourceSequence\", a)),\n+            And(convergence, algebraic));\n+    }\n+\n+    private static Formula Octic(Formula x) => Add(Sub(Sub(Sub(Pow(x, D(8)), Pow(x, D(6))), Pow(x, D(4))), Pow(x, D(2))), D(1));\n+    private static DocumentBlock Node(string name, string title, Formula formula, string prose,\n+        DescribeRole role, AssessedProvenance provenance, OpenProblemResolutionClaim? resolution = null) => Describe.Lean(\n+        DescribeId.Create(\"oeis-a400645-\" + name.ToLowerInvariant()), DeclarationHandle.Create(Prefix + name),\n+        H(title), StatementSource.FromAuthor(Disp(formula)), provenance, Blocks(Paragraph(Text(prose))), role, resolution);\n+    private static Formula V(string name) => F.Id(name);\n+    private static Formula Named(string name) => Seq(Operatorname, Grp(V(name)));\n+    private static Formula Q(string owner, string name) => Seq(Named(owner), Dot, Named(name));\n+    private static Formula Call(string name, params Formula[] arguments) => new Formula.Apply(Named(name), [.. arguments]);\n+    private static Formula SqrtOf(Formula value) => new Formula.Apply(Q(\"Real\", \"sqrt\"), [value]);\n+    private static Formula Nat() => Seq(Mathbb, Grp(V(\"N\")));\n+    private static Formula Int() => Seq(Mathbb, Grp(V(\"Z\")));\n+    private static Formula Real() => Seq(Mathbb, Grp(V(\"R\")));\n+    private static Formula SequenceType() => Seq(Nat(), Sp, To, Sp, Nat());\n+    private static Formula Parenthesized(Formula value) => Seq(Open, value, Close);\n+    private static Formula Cast(Formula value, Formula type) => Parenthesized(Seq(value, Colon, Sp, type));\n+    private static Formula All(string name, Formula type, Formula body) => Seq(Forall, Sp, V(name), Colon, Sp, Parenthesized(type), Comma, Sp, body);\n+    private static Formula ExistsOf(string name, Formula type, Formula body) => Seq(Exists, Sp, V(name), Colon, Sp, Parenthesized(type), Comma, Sp, body);\n+    private static Formula Equal(Formula x, Formula y) => new Formula.Relation(x, FormulaRelationOperator.Equal, y);\n+    private static Formula Le(Formula x, Formula y) => new Formula.Relation(x, FormulaRelationOperator.LessThanOrEqual, y);\n+    private static Formula Lt(Formula x, Formula y) => new Formula.Relation(x, FormulaRelationOperator.LessThan, y);\n+    private static Formula And(Formula x, Formula y) => new Formula.Logic(Parenthesized(x), FormulaLogicOperator.And, Parenthesized(y));\n+    private static Formula Imp(Formula x, Formula y) => new Formula.Logic(Parenthesized(x), FormulaLogicOperator.Implies, Parenthesized(y));\n+    private static Formula Add(Formula x, Formula y) => Seq(x, Sp, Plus, Sp, y);\n+    private static Formula Sub(Formula x, Formula y) => Seq(x, Sp, Minus, Sp, y);\n+    private static Formula Mul(Formula x, Formula y) => Seq(x, Sp, Cdot, Sp, y);\n+    private static Formula Divide(Formula x, Formula y) => new Formula.Fraction(x, y);\n+    private static Formula Pow(Formula x, Formula y) => new Formula.Power(Parenthesized(x), y);\n+    private static Formula Abs(Formula x) => Seq(Lvert, Sp, x, Sp, Rvert);\n+}"},{"sha":"33314cf90d7d734d1125024ec87b2b7e8ac13607","filename":"D5/S1/Recurrence/OEISA400644.lean","status":"modified","additions":10,"deletions":1,"changes":11,"blob_url":"https://github.com/the-omega-institute/trureturing/blob/3a382196d3b69fec4a2ba29a7468eca5e9844034/D5%2FS1%2FRecurrence%2FOEISA400644.lean","raw_url":"https://github.com/the-omega-institute/trureturing/raw/3a382196d3b69fec4a2ba29a7468eca5e9844034/D5%2FS1%2FRecurrence%2FOEISA400644.lean","contents_url":"https://